~ start
if Global.son_dialogue_progress == 0:
	S: Woah! Who are you?
	
	PC: Alright, who lost their kid?
	PC: (This train is insane…)
	
	PC: (I don’t have time for this.)
	PC: “No, kid, I don’t.”

	$> Global.son_dialogue_progress = 1
	=> END
if Global.son_dialogue_progress == 1:
	if Global.has_messy_music_sheet == true:
		S: *Gasps* “You found my song! Yay!”

		PC: “You mean this piece of-”

		S: “Thank you so so much, Mister! Can I play it for you as a gift?”
		S: “Mama told me that I have a hidden talent for music and that my songs are a gift to the world and that she’s proud of me and that Papa should be too and-“

		PC: (At this rate, he should keep his talent hidden. Now that would be a proper gift to the world.)

		S: “-and even though he is super busy all the time I know he cares because he got me a xylophone and-”
		S: “Wait. I don’t have my xylophone. Mister, could you please please please get me one with a cherry on top?”

		PC: “If it means you’ll be quiet again, then fine.”

		S: “Woohooo!”

		#Flashback
		#$> Global.fade_in()
		#$> Global.show_memorabilia("messy_music_sheet")

		#$> Global.hide_memorabilia()
		#$> Global.fade_out()
		#Flashback end
		
		$> Global.son_dialogue_progress = 2
		=> END
	else:
		S: Hi, Mister!

		PC: (I don’t have time for this.)
		=> END
if Global.son_dialogue_progress == 2:
	if Global.has_xylophone == true:
		S: “Thanks again for the present, Mister!”

		PC: “Stop calling me that.“

		S: “Here goes nothing!”

		#Flashback
		$> Global.fade_in()
		$> Global.show_memorabilia("xylophone")
		
		PC: (Haven’t I heard this before? Not all of it is familiar, but this melody…)
		PC: (It must have been what my wife recorded at his recital. The one I missed because I had to work overtime.)
		PC: (Or was I drinking? I can’t remember. Probably drinking in that case.) 
		PC: (This song sounds just as bad as my first time hearing it, at least the first few seconds I bothered listening to before losing interest. 
		PC: (Is that my fault for not getting a better instrument? He should be grateful that he has one at all.) 
		PC: (Or does it suck because I wasn't there for him to teach him a lesson? Forget it, forget everything. No one listens to what I have to say anyway.)
		PC: (Yes. Forget it all. But still… he exists, and I’m fading. In that case, forget me.)
		PC: (But what if…)
		
		$> Global.hide_memorabilia()
		$> Global.fade_out()
		#Flashback end

		S: “Mist- sorry, um, sir. Why are you crying?”

		PC: “I’m not. I’m just feeling sleepy, is all.”

		S: *Continues playing*

		PC: “Are you trying to torture me?! ”
		PC: “Don’t you have anyone else to perform for?”

		S: “Yeah! At school, I’m going to show this song to everyone and it’ll be awesome! I can’t wait to see Papa there too, even if I don’t know what he looks like very well. Mama said not to get my hopes up, but the last time I saw him, he made a pinky promise with me.“
		S: “Mama said that he always breaks his promises, but he made a pinky promise with me, which is super special and means he won’t break it no matter what.”

		PC: “You know, I have an idea where your Papa might be.”

		S: “Really?”

		PC: “Yes. I can find him before your school performance starts. In fact, when does it start?”

		S: “Next week. Here’s one of the handouts my teacher gave me for the concert. I gave one to Mama already, and since you can find Papa, you can have it!”

		PC: “Great. How kind.”

		Game: School Concert Handout obtained.

		PC: “I promise I’ll find your Papa, so that we’ll both get what we want.”

		S: “Pinky promise?”

		PC: “Pinky promise.”
		
		$> Global.son_dialogue_progress = 3
		=> END
	else:
		S: Mister, could you please please please get me a xylophone. Pretty please with a cherry on top?”
=> END